S = {'cc': 'PA', 'fam': 'Capital', 'doc': "# PA 2025: capital income and gains of households (1100), stacked on the 1.x model\n\nThe 1.x model (vendored unchanged; its statute sources and grades are in its own `results/summary.json`) taxes the\nhousehold's `interest`, `dividends`, `rentalIncome` and `capitalGains` (the contract: gains on long-held listed\nshares). A global line's **additional** items of exactly those kinds (income items `interest`, `dividend`, `rent`;\ndisposals of listed shares held over 12 months) are routed into those fields and charged as the 1.x income tax with\nthem less the 1.x income tax without them (kernel `stackedTax`, DESIGN §6). Gains on real estate, unlisted shares and\nshort holdings, and other income kinds, need the country's own gains rules: listed as unsupported (not computed).", 'lean': 'def capF : Family := stackFamily pitOf "1.x model income tax on household interest, dividends, rentalIncome, capitalGains (stackedTax)"', 'families': '[capF]', 'guards': ['example (args : List String) (c : Canon) : capF.run args (CanonGlobal.ofCanon c) [] = [] := stackFamily_legacy _ _ args c []', '(capF.run [] { id := "g", household := { id := "g" } } []).length == 0'], 'taxes': [{'oecd': '1100', 'tax': 'Income tax on additional interest, dividends, rent and listed-share gains (stacked)', 'statute': '1.x model (see its summary.json); kernel stackedTax', 'dated': 'as the 1.x model (2025)', 'grade': 'B', 'package': 'P3', 'kernel_parts': ['stackedTax', 'addToRaw'], 'unsupported': ['real estate, unlisted shares and short-held gains rules', 'other income kinds']}], 'unsupported_expr': 'stackUnsupported g'}
